## Context

The review of #4471 found separate parser and booking-form hint failures in one ticket.
The same subject can describe different causes; different subjects can describe the same
cause. Intake tags can disagree with the tenant directory and channel.

## Decision

This record supersedes [decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) for this
review's triage guidance. The accepted historical record remains unchanged. This exported
KB does not itself deploy any change to the live support desk.

Read the report body and identify the affected product, tenant, tenant locale, booking form
and entry path. For these date reports, use `causeOf` from `src/lib/kb/causes.ts` with the
tenant directory, not the browser locale or guessed tag. Merge only when the failure cause
matches. Treat subject matching as a way to find candidates, never as proof.

Do not merge unknown or contradictory reports automatically. Request missing evidence and
keep an explicit investigation record. The date classifier covers this incident; it is not
a classifier for every product the desk supports.

## Consequences

The desk must read more before merging. Engineering gets separate problems with distinct
report counts and fixes. Export overlaps must be deduplicated by report ID before counting.
Any later change to this decision needs a new record rather than an edit to accepted history.

